<%- include('partials/layout-head', { title: 'Something broke' }) %>
<div class="rounded-lg border border-dashed border-red-900/60 px-6 py-16 text-center">
  <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">Something broke while building this page.</p>
  <%# The exception text is deliberately not printed here. It carries the
      absolute path of whatever file it was reading, which puts a home directory
      and a username into a page that gets screenshotted -- the same reason the
      footer shows the data directory home-relative. The terminal running the
      server has the whole thing, stack included. %>
  <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-slate-500">
    The details are in the terminal running the server. A damaged file in the
    data directory is the usual cause.
  </p>
  <a href="<%= u('/') %>" class="mt-4 inline-block text-sm text-sky-400 hover:underline">Back to invoices</a>
</div>
<%- include('partials/layout-foot') %>
